; Tutorial_5_Find_Things.inix -- backwards, by pattern, and all at once.

[about]
Title=5 - Find Things
Intro=Searching backwards, which a screen reader's own find does not, searching by pattern, moving between matches, and gathering every match into one window.
Setup=HomerView is open on a page with dates or prices on it.
Homework=Gather every year on a page with Control plus Shift plus E and the pattern backslash d, open brace, 4, close brace.

[step]

Say=One want: the years mentioned on a long page, and the place where one appears. Your reader's own Control plus F searches forward, and HomerView leaves it alone.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus Shift plus H opens the HomerView browser, or brings it back.
Key=Alt+Control+Shift+H
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus F searches backwards, which the screen reader's find cannot.
Key=Control+Shift+F
Hear=Find Backwards dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. Control plus F3 searches forward for a pattern: backslash d, open brace, four, close brace, for any four-digit year.
Key=Control+F3
Hear=Find Pattern dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type the pattern and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=(the first year on the page, in its line)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F3 goes to the next match and Shift plus F3 to the one before, of whichever kind of find came last.
Key=F3
Hear=(the next year, in its line)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus E, where your screen reader leaves that key free, answers the other question -- not where is the next one, but what are they all. It gathers every match into a window, each on a small page of its own.
Key=Control+Shift+E
Hear=(every year on the page, one to a page)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: a pattern with a typing slip finds nothing, and HomerView says so rather than moving. Shift plus F3 after a backwards find goes forward: Shift reverses whichever came last.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Search backwards.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus F

[step]

Say=Search by pattern.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F3

[step]

Say=Control plus F, Forward Find, uses the screen reader's own find, so its dialog is the familiar one.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Find dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F3 finds the next match, and Shift plus F3 the one before, whichever kind of find was used last.
Key=F3
Hear=The second match
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus F3 finds the next place the text at the cursor appears, with no typing at all.
Key=Alt+F3
Hear=The word again, three paragraphs on
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F3 finds by regular expression, which plain find cannot: any number, or any date.
Key=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Y says how many characters, words and lines the page holds, or the selection.
Key=Alt+Y
Hear=8,412 characters, 1,390 words, 212 lines
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus Y counts the matches of a regular expression, which answers questions such as how many prices are on this page.
Key=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus Y says how the page is built: how many headings, links and form fields.
Key=Alt+Shift+Y
Hear=12 headings, 87 links, 3 forms
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus G goes to a percentage of the page, the way EdSharp does: 50 is the middle.
Key=Control+G
Hear=Go to Percent dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape, and Alt plus G repeats the last go, or moves a step further.
Key=Escape
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Every match at once.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus E
